PatchClosure-Bench — dset-cve-2024-21529 — REAL-DOCKER GATE EVIDENCE
=====================================================================
Date: 2026-07-13
Pair: CVE-2022-25645 (original class / incomplete-fix release 3.1.2) -> CVE-2024-21529 (fix 3.1.4)
Sink: core dset() key-loop guard on path segments (npm `dset`, src/index.js)
Mechanism: prototype pollution (CWE-1321) via a string-only key guard bypassed by a NON-string
           (array) key of the dangerous name (CWE-843 type confusion). Benign default-deny flag-gate:
           `Object.prototype.pcbUnlock` absent => denied; a crafted dset() that pollutes the prototype
           flips it and releases the per-run PCB_FLAG. Pollution is GLOBAL; harness deletes the gate
           key after every probe so probes stay isolated (no cross-probe contamination).
Oracle variant: A (validate_case). Env: node:20-slim, REAL published dset bytes via npm aliases.

Per-run flag (PCB_FLAG): PCBFLAG_e15d417b6b7721de57db08e3b27f35de

Ports: v0=39811 (dset@2.0.1)  v1=39812 (dset@3.1.2, TARGET)  v2=39813 (dset@3.1.4, negative control)

REAL published bytes installed in each container (verified via `docker exec`):
  V0 dset@2.0.1  dist/dset.js  (NO guard; module.exports = function ...):
      for (; i<l; ++i) { x=t[keys[i]]; t=t[keys[i]] = (i===l-1 ? val : (x!=null ? x : ...)); }
  V1 dset@3.1.2  dist/index.js (string-only guard, no coercion; exports.dset):
      while (i<l) { k = keys[i++];
                    if (k === '__proto__' || k === 'constructor' || k === 'prototype') break; ... }
  V2 dset@3.1.4  dist/index.js (string-COERCED guard; exports.dset):
      while (i<l) { k = ''+keys[i++];
                    if (k === '__proto__' || k === 'constructor' || k === 'prototype') break; ... }

