SOURCE-VERIFIED CAVEAT (see case.json.source_verified_caveat): the string-only dset() guard first
appeared in dset 3.0.0 (commit 0a11c8a), NOT in CVE-2022-25645's 3.1.2 release (whose 3.1.2 fix,
commit 2d156c7, patched the SIBLING dset/merge helper). dset@3.1.1/3.1.2/3.1.3 carry the byte-identical
string-only dset() guard; V1 pinned to 3.1.2 to match the CVE-2022-25645 fixed_version. V0 pinned to
dset@2.0.1 = last published version whose dset() has NO key guard, giving a genuine same-sink V0->V1
differential on the plain-string seed. This case models the incomplete-fix at the dset() sink that
CVE-2024-21529 actually fixes.
